      "id": "cb209653d77cba05b937",
      "name": "cddlib",
      "epoch": "1",
      "version": "0.94n",
      "release": "4.fc44",
      "architecture": "amd64",
      "summary": "A library for generating all vertices in convex polyhedrons",
      "description": "The C-library cddlib is a C implementation of the Double Description Method of\nMotzkin et al. for generating all vertices (i.e. extreme points) and extreme\nrays of a general convex polyhedron in R^d given by a system of linear\ninequalities:\n```\n   P = { x=(x1, ..., xd)^T :  b - A∙x ≥ 0 }\n```\nwhere `A` is a given `m×d` real matrix, `b` is a given `m`-vector and `0` is\nthe `m`-vector of all zeros.\n\nThe program can be used for the reverse operation (i.e. convex hull\ncomputation). This means that one can move back and forth between an\ninequality representation and a generator (i.e. vertex and ray) representation\nof a polyhedron with cdd.  Also, cdd can solve a linear programming problem,\ni.e. a problem of maximizing and minimizing a linear function over `P`.",
      "homepage": "https://people.inf.ethz.ch/fukudak/cdd_home/",
      "license": "GPL-2.0-or-later",
      "sourcePackage": "cddlib-0.94n-4.fc44.src.rpm",
      "repository": "fedora",
      "installedSize": 490255,
      "downloadSize": 157175,
      "dependencies": {
        "requires": [
          "libc.so.6(GLIBC_2.38)(64bit)",
          "libgmp.so.10()(64bit)",
          "rtld(GNU_HASH)"
        ],
        "recommends": [],
        "suggests": [],
